    <!-- Section 2: Service Description & Free Model -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">02.</span>
        Description of the Service &amp; Free Model
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        3DPrintingCostCalc.com provides independent, browser-based computational
        utilities for the additive manufacturing community. These include
        filament weight converters, electricity cost amortizations, 3D printer
        total cost of ownership (TCO) estimators, spool tare weight databases,
        multicolor AMS waste estimators, and SLA/resin volume calculations.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        The Service is offered completely free of charge on an
        &ldquo;AS-IS&rdquo; and &ldquo;AS-AVAILABLE&rdquo; basis. We reserve the
        right to modify, enhance, update, or discontinue features of the Service
        at any time without notice or liability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Engineering Calculations & Mathematical Disclaimer -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">03.</span>
        Engineering Calculations &amp; Mathematical Estimation Disclaimer
      </h2>
      <div
        class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-950/30 border border-amber-500/40 text-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2"
      >
        <p class="font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-300">
          Important Engineering &amp; Operational Notice:
        </p>
        <p>
          Additive manufacturing processes depend on complex, non-linear
          physical variables that cannot be predicted with mathematical
          perfection outside calibrated laboratory conditions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm">
        You acknowledge that all calculation results, cost breakdowns, weight
        estimations, print duration forecasts, and electricity rates generated
        by 3DPrintingCostCalc.com are <strong
          >theoretical mathematical estimates and planning benchmarks only</strong
        >. Real-world 3D printing results vary significantly due to factors
        including:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm pl-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Polymer Density &amp; Batch Variances:</strong> Raw filament and
          resin densities vary by manufacturer and color pigments (&plusmn;3% to &plusmn;5%).
          Hygroscopic moisture absorption also alters physical filament mass.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Filament Diameter Tolerances:</strong> Standard 1.75mm spools fluctuate
          between 1.72mm and 1.78mm (&plusmn;0.03mm), changing extruded volume per
          linear meter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Slicer Algorithms &amp; Acceleration Curves:</strong> Actual print
          times are governed by physical stepper motor kinematics, acceleration, jerk,
          resonance compensation (input shaping), wipe towers, and nozzle purge volumes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Thermal &amp; Power Factors:</strong> Ambient chamber temperatures,
          draft conditions, heated bed thermal loss, and regional electricity tariffs
          fluctuate continuously.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm">
        <strong>Mandatory User Verification:</strong> You are solely responsible for
        conducting physical test prints, weighing spools and finished prints on calibrated
        digital scales, verifying toolpath slices in your machine slicer, and confirming
        economic viability before entering into commercial quoting, Etsy order fulfillment,
        or mass manufacturing runs.
      </p>
    </section>

